course: dictionary
lesson: 4464
title: Hardship and hardships
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hardship is a noun for a hard time, when you suffer because you have too little money, food or other things you need. In «Toad sobs that he will go out into the dark night to share their hardships», hardships means several difficult times that friends have shared.
explain: The ending -s matters. Hardship names the whole situation, while hardships means more than one difficulty. Clue words help too: «financial hardship» tells you the trouble is about money, and «face hardship» tells you someone has to deal with it.
explain: Context shows the meaning. In Toad's words, the hardships come before the happy ending, when «Supper's here at last, hooray!» Chinese has a similar idea: in «chī kǔ», chī means eat and kǔ means bitter, and together they mean to put up with hardship.
fact: Hardship means a situation of suffering or difficulty, often from not having enough money, food or things you need.
fact: A hardship is one particular difficulty that makes life hard.
fact: «Financial hardship» means hard times caused by not having enough money.
fact: A «hardship fund» is money set aside to help people who are struggling.
fact: In history, people faced hardship during war and famine, such as rationing in the Second World War.
exercise: «Families may face financial hardship if a parent loses a job.» What does financial hardship mean? | *Hard times caused by not having enough money | A school trip to the seaside | A new job for a parent | A big family party
exercise: Find and copy the word that means several difficulties in «Toad sobs that he will go out into the dark night to share their hardships». | share | night | dishes | *hardships
exercise: In stories, characters often overcome hardship. What does overcome hardship mean? | Forget a hard time completely | Avoid every book with a sad ending | *Get through a hard time | Cause a hard time for others
test: «The family lived through great hardship during the war.» What does great hardship mean? | A loud noise in the street | Very good luck | *Very hard times with too little food | Long journeys by train
test: Why might a school have a hardship fund? | To buy new computers only | To pay for a swimming pool | *To help families who are struggling | To give extra holidays to everyone
exam: Which is the best meaning of hardship? | A loud argument between friends | A happy surprise | *Suffering or difficulty, especially from lacking money, food or other things you need | A wet, grey day
